WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:19.443
Unit eleven: B2 First: Overview and Use of English Cloze. Today you will understand the B2 First exam and complete multiple-choice and open cloze tasks.

4
00:00:19.743 --> 00:00:22.267
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:26.280
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:28.141
Collocation.

7
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.893
Collocation means words that often go together.

8
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:34.634
Make a decision is a collocation.

9
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.007
Your turn. Say: Collocation.

10
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:41.984
Collocation.

11
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.832
Phrasal verb.

12
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:47.850
Phrasal verb means a verb with a particle, like give up.

13
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.229
Give up is a phrasal verb.

14
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.550
Your turn. Say: Phrasal verb.

15
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.401
Phrasal verb.

16
00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.244
Fixed phrase.

17
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.364
Fixed phrase means a group of words that does not change.

18
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.008
As a result is a fixed phrase.

19
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:09.292
Your turn. Say: Fixed phrase.

20
00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.703
Fixed phrase.

21
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.207
Meaning.

22
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:18.576
Meaning means what a word or phrase says.

23
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:20.219
Check the meaning.

24
00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:23.132
Your turn. Say: Meaning.

25
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:26.898
Meaning.

26
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.814
Grammar word.

27
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:32.884
Grammar word means a word like of, the or which.

28
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:35.738
Open cloze needs grammar words.

29
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.014
Your turn. Say: Grammar word.

30
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.204
Grammar word.

31
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.881
Option.

32
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:48.069
Option means one possible answer.

33
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:50.242
Choose the best option.

34
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.479
Your turn. Say: Option.

35
00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:57.276
Option.

36
00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.006
Contrast.

37
00:02:00.017 --> 00:02:01.889
Contrast means a difference.

38
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:04.344
The text shows a contrast.

39
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.695
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

40
00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:11.592
Contrast.

41
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.815
Relative pronoun.

42
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:17.815
Relative pronoun means a word like which or who.

43
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:19.917
Use which for things.

44
00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:23.587
Your turn. Say: Relative pronoun.

45
00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:27.922
Relative pronoun.

46
00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:32.535
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:35.453
Visal, what is B2 First?

48
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:50.661
B2 First is a Cambridge exam at upper-intermediate level. Reading and Use of English is one paper with seven parts, and then there are Writing, Listening and Speaking papers.

49
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.842
What happens in the first two parts?

50
00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:07.355
Part 1 is a multiple-choice cloze: you choose the best word for each gap from four options. Part 2 is an open cloze where you write one word in each gap.

51
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.461
How can I improve my accuracy?

52
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:26.567
For Part 1 learn collocations, phrasal verbs and fixed phrases. For Part 2 learn grammar words such as articles, prepositions, auxiliary verbs, relative pronouns and linking words.

53
00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:29.234
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:34.080
Grammar focus: Strategy: meaning and grammar together.

55
00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.590
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:38.782
She made a decision, not did a decision.

57
00:03:39.683 --> 00:03:42.693
The book, which I bought yesterday, is excellent.

58
00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:51.617
Read the whole text first. For Part 1 test each option for meaning and collocation. For Part 2 decide which grammar word is missing.

59
00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:56.824
Be careful! Don't say: I choose a word without checking the collocation.

60
00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.778
Say: I check the collocation.

61
00:04:01.078 --> 00:04:02.532
Check collocations.

62
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.753
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:07.858
Cloze Practice.

64
00:04:08.158 --> 00:04:10.843
Pich practises a multiple-choice cloze.

65
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:14.007
The gap comes before the word decision.

66
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.534
She knows that make is the correct collocation.

67
00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:22.251
In the open cloze the next gap needs the relative pronoun which.

68
00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:25.510
She reads each sentence again to check.

69
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.520
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:31.383 --> 00:04:33.963
How many parts in Reading and Use of English?

71
00:04:34.263 --> 00:04:37.383
A, two. B, twelve. C, seven.

72
00:04:40.933 --> 00:04:43.003
The answer is C: seven.

73
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.964
Part 2 is an blank cloze.

74
00:04:46.264 --> 00:04:49.639
A, open. B, closed. C, multiple.

75
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.188
The answer is A: open.

76
00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.315
Which collocation is correct?

77
00:04:58.615 --> 00:05:04.230
A, take a decision always. B, make a decision. C, do a decision.

78
00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.579
The answer is B: make a decision.

79
00:05:11.717 --> 00:05:13.856
Which pronoun refers to a thing?

80
00:05:14.156 --> 00:05:17.101
A, who. B, whom. C, which.

81
00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.666
The answer is C: which.

82
00:05:23.817 --> 00:05:25.642
After choosing, you should blank.

83
00:05:25.942 --> 00:05:29.712
A, read the sentence again. B, stop. C, skip.

84
00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:35.812
The answer is A: read the sentence again.

85
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.140
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:40.983 --> 00:05:43.227
How do you approach the cloze tasks?

87
00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.633
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:53.933 --> 00:06:07.142
I read the whole text for the general meaning. In Part 1 I test each option with its collocation or phrasal verb. In Part 2 I decide which grammar word is missing and read the sentence again to check.

89
00:06:07.442 --> 00:06:09.116
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:10.017 --> 00:06:15.142
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: meaning and grammar together.

91
00:06:15.442 --> 00:06:20.265
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:20.565 --> 00:06:23.160
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.984
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

